#=============================================================================
# puf_lock.xdc -- Butterfly PUF: let the cross-coupled LUT loops through
#
# NOTE: keep this file ASCII-only.
#
# ============================ TWO HARD LESSONS ===============================
#
# 1) XDC constraint files are NOT general Tcl.
#    Vivado parses them with a restricted constraint parser that REJECTS
#    control flow. A version of this file wrapped things in "if {[catch {...}]}"
#    and Vivado reported:
#      CRITICAL WARNING: [Designutils 20-1307] Command 'if' is not supported
#                        in the xdc constraint file. [puf_lock.xdc:38]
#    The block was SILENTLY SKIPPED. Rule for this file: PLAIN CONSTRAINTS ONLY.
#    No if / catch / foreach / while / proc / puts / set-variables.
#
# 2) The severity override is NOT how this DRC is bypassed.
#    "set_property SEVERITY {Warning} [get_drc_checks LUTLP-1]" was tried, and
#    it was even injected INSIDE the run sub-processes via
#    STEPS.<STEP>.TCL.PRE (confirmed: each step logged
#      "source .../drc_relax_pre.tcl"), yet write_bitstream still failed with
#    128 LUTLP-1 errors ("Bitgen not run").
#    Vivado's own DRC message states the supported bypass:
#      "... this DRC can be bypassed by acknowledging the condition and setting
#       the following XDC constraint on any one of the nets in the loop:
#         set_property ALLOW_COMBINATORIAL_LOOPS TRUE [get_nets <myHier/myNet>]"
#    So the fix is a NET property, applied to one net inside each loop.
#    The RTL-level (* ALLOW_COMBINATORIAL_LOOPS = "TRUE" *) attribute on the
#    module was NOT enough -- the netlist net needs the property.
#
# ======================= WHY THE LOOPS EXIST AT ALL ==========================
#    A Butterfly PUF cell IS a cross-coupled pair of LUTs, i.e. a combinational
#    loop by construction (force both nodes, release, let the cell settle
#    according to manufacturing mismatch -> one bit of chip fingerprint).
#    This DRC firing is expected for a PUF, not a defect.
#
#    Cell hierarchy in the synthesized/placed netlist (confirmed from the DRC
#    message itself):
#      up_proj_i/puf_bd_0/inst/u_array/g_cell[<N>].u_cell
#    Nets in the loop: .../u_cell/a and .../u_cell/b
#    We allow the loop on the "a" net of every cell (128 cells, N = 0..127).
#=============================================================================


#-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1) Downgrade the combinatorial-loop DRC (harmless, keeps reports readable).
#
#    NOTE: this alone does NOT let bitgen through -- see below.
#-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
set_property SEVERITY {Warning} [get_drc_checks LUTLP-1]


#-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2) Why the loop is NOT suppressed here
#
#    The real suppression is "set_property ALLOW_COMBINATORIAL_LOOPS TRUE" on a
#    NET, which Vivado's own DRC message prescribes. That CANNOT be expressed
#    reliably in this XDC file, for two measured reasons:
#
#      a) XDC rejects control flow (no foreach), so we would have to name the
#         nets with a pattern.
#      b) The name pattern DID NOT MATCH. Measured 2026-10-13:
#           WARNING: [Vivado 12-507] No nets matched
#                    'up_proj_i/puf_bd_0/inst/u_array/g_cell[*]/u_cell/a'
#           ERROR: [Common 17-55] 'set_property' expects at least one object
#         and that error aborted opt_design at 20%.
#
#    So the net property is applied from a Tcl script instead, which the run
#    sub-processes DO execute:
#        constr/drc_relax_pre.tcl   (generated by tools/puf_p1_synth.tcl)
#        attached via STEPS.<STEP>.TCL.PRE on impl_1
#    That script loops over the REAL PUF cells and their real nets, so it needs
#    no pattern matching at all. Delivery is proven: the run log shows
#        source .../constr/drc_relax_pre.tcl
#    inside each step sub-process.
#
#    Keep this XDC free of any get_nets pattern for LUTLP-1 -- a non-matching
#    get_nets here turns into a hard error and can abort a run step.
#-----------------------------------------------------------------------------


#-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3) Placement freeze of the PUF array
#
#    A PUF's response is determined by the PHYSICAL implementation. Re-synthesis
#    or re-placement changes the response, which permanently invalidates every
#    ciphertext and helper data produced earlier. So placement must be frozen.
#
#    The pblock commands live in a SEPARATE file, constr/puf_pblock.xdc, which
#    tools/puf_lock_from_place.tcl generates AUTOMATICALLY after the first
#    implementation -- the pblock needs real SLICE coordinates and guessing them
#    is unreliable.
#
#    Workflow:
#      1) implement once WITHOUT the pblock
#      2) open_run impl_1 ; source tools/puf_lock_from_place.tcl
#         -> writes constr/puf_pblock.xdc with literal commands
#      3) re-run tools/add_puf_to_bd.tcl (adds puf_pblock.xdc if present)
#      4) re-run tools/puf_p1_synth.tcl -> placement now frozen
#      5) verify: two independent builds must give a bit-identical response
#-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# (intentionally empty here -- the pblock is in constr/puf_pblock.xdc)
